# Overview

This document provides a complete reference for the command-line interface (CLI) of **swot-reservoir-wse**. 
---

# Command Overview

The package currently provides four primary command groups.

| Command   | Purpose                                                                |
| --------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `polygon` | Generate reservoir-specific Water Surface Elevation (WSE) time series. |
| `auth`    | Configure and authenticate Google Earth Engine.                        |
| `config`  | View and modify package configuration.                                 |
| `cache`   | Inspect and manage cached files.                                       |

Display all available commands using

```bash
swot-wse --help
```

---

# 1. Polygon Command

The `polygon` command is the primary entry point of the package. It extracts a Water Surface Elevation (WSE) time series for a reservoir using user-supplied coordinates and a date range.

## Syntax

```bash
swot-wse polygon --lat <latitude> --lon <longitude> --start-date YYYY-MM-DD --end-date YYYY-MM-DD [--source <source>]
```

## Arguments

| Argument       | Required | Description                                   |
| -------------- | :------: | --------------------------------------------- |
| `--lat`        |    Yes   | Latitude of the reservoir or dam location.    |
| `--lon`        |    Yes   | Longitude of the reservoir or dam location.   |
| `--start-date` |    Yes   | Beginning of the observation period.          |
| `--end-date`   |    Yes   | End of the observation period.                |
| `--source`     |    No    | Observation source to use. Default is `auto`. |

## Example

```bash
swot-wse polygon --lat 19.690 --lon 73.340 --start-date 2026-01-20 --end-date 2026-07-16
```

## Source Selection

The package is designed around a source abstraction layer.

Current implementation:

| Source   | Status                                   |
| -------- | ---------------------------------------- |
| `auto`   | Supported (currently resolves to LakeSP) |          

Future releases may extend `auto` to select from multiple supported SWOT observation products.

