# 3. Configuration Commands

Package behaviour is controlled through the configuration system.

## Display Current Configuration

```bash
swot-wse config show
```

Displays the complete runtime configuration currently used by the package.

---

## Modify a Configuration Parameter

```bash
swot-wse config set <parameter> <value>
```

Examples

```bash
swot-wse config set generate_plot false
```

```bash
swot-wse config set search_radius_m 100000
```

```bash
swot-wse config set working_crs EPSG:32721
```

```bash
swot-wse config set polygon_cache_enabled false
```

```bash
swot-wse config set lakesp_cache_enabled false
```

```bash
swot-wse config set output_dir outputs
```

Nested configuration values are also supported.

Example

```bash
swot-wse config set sources.lakesp.mad_threshold 2.5
```

List-valued parameters must be supplied as JSON lists.

Example

```bash
swot-wse config set sources.lakesp.science_cycles '["045","046","047"]'
```

---

## Reset Configuration

```bash
swot-wse config reset
```

Restores the package configuration to the default values defined by the current release.

---

# Configurable Parameters

## General Parameters

| Parameter               | Description                                    |
| ----------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- |
| `earth_engine_project`  | Google Earth Engine Project ID.                |
| `search_radius_m`       | Search radius used for reservoir extraction.   |
| `pekel_threshold`       | JRC Global Surface Water occurrence threshold. |
| `working_crs`           | CRS used for area and distance calculations.   |
| `max_workers`           | Maximum number of worker threads.              |
| `generate_plot`         | Enable or disable PNG generation.              |
| `polygon_cache_enabled` | Enable or disable reservoir polygon caching.   |
| `lakesp_cache_enabled`  | Enable or disable LakeSP granule caching.      |
| `cache_dir`             | Root cache directory.                          |
| `output_dir`            | Output directory.                              |
| `temp_download_dir`     | Temporary download workspace.                  |

---

## LakeSP Parameters

| Parameter                              | Description                                       |
| -------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------- |
| `sources.lakesp.collection`            | NASA Earthdata LakeSP collection identifier.      |
| `sources.lakesp.search_buffer_degrees` | Search buffer applied during product discovery.   |
| `sources.lakesp.science_cycles`        | SWOT science cycles included during discovery.    |
| `sources.lakesp.mad_threshold`         | Modified Z-score threshold used during filtering. |

